-- rust: reject [E1002] pinned 2026-08-12 — the code this file has always
--       produced; previously unpinned, so ANY diagnostic satisfied it.
-- gate: reject
-- defect: duplicate top-level binding `x` (redefinition in one module)
-- oracle: reject — Sky has no multi-clause definitions; the oracle emits Go
--         that `go build` rejects ("x redeclared in this block").
--
-- The Rust resolver used to last-wins-overwrite the second `x` silently
-- (IndexMap::insert + interned DefId collision), so `sky check` accepted a
-- program `go build` refuses — a `sky check ≡ sky build` violation. Fixed in
-- `hir::resolve::register_locals`: a repeated top-level value name emits
-- `[E1002]`, gated before lower/emit by the driver's name-error halt.
module Main exposing (main)

import Sky.Core.Prelude exposing (..)
import Std.Log exposing (println)

x = 1
x = 2

main =
    println (String.fromInt x)